    <http://example.org/node/chunk94> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Evaluation criteria Offers will be evaluated against the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution; compliance with regulatory requirements; level of security; data sovereignty; quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI; total cost of the proposed solution; consideration of environmental issues; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk95> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff, serving a regional hospital (approximately 1,200 beds and 4,500 staff), with objectives to improve efficiency, quality, and safety." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk96> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution must provide an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the work environment, supporting clinical-administrative activities without introducing rupture in workflows." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk97> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's PM methodologies, past public sector references, consortium partners, available capacity, and governance practices as of 2024, how do our company's plan to coordinate this project while ensuring decision traceability? our company's will coordinate this project using our company's Hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement. this project will be divided into phases: Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run, each ending with a formal review and a go/no-go decision." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk98> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given The client requirements for an intelligent assistance tool supporting clinical-administrative activities without introducing rupture in workflows, our company's believe our company's flagship product Atelier can provide a sovereign platform that forges document-grounded AI assistants from the hospital's own documents. a sovereign platform that forges document-grounded AI assistants from the hospital's own documents has been successfully implemented in past public sector references, such as with a regional council and a mutual health insurer. our company's consortium partners, including OuraneCloud for hosting on a French sovereign cloud provider (SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified) and Ligeo Santé for health-IT integration, will support this project. our company's also have a joint research programme with a French public AI research laboratory on retrieval-augmented generation and explainability, which may bring additional value to the solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk99> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of available capacity, our company's can dedicate a team consisting of a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead, ensuring that all aspects of this project are covered. our company's governance practices include a joint steering committee (Faber IA + client), meeting monthly, and an operational committee meeting fortnightly, ensuring decision traceability and clear communication." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

